        "pt": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "# 📊 China Coffee Chain Market: Luckin vs. Starbucks Business Model Analysis\n\n> This report delivers an in-depth evaluation of single-store unit economics, cost structures, and supply chain strategies for two leading coffee giants to support cafe site selection.\n\n## 1. Core Strategy & Positioning Comparison\n\n- **Starbucks**: Focuses on the \"Third Space\" social experience. Average store footprint: 150-250 ㎡ with high lease costs, relying on premium ticket sizes (¥35-45).\n- **Luckin Coffee**: Focuses on \"Pick-up outlets\" and digital app ordering. Average store footprint: 20-50 ㎡ with high sales density and viral product hit rates (e.g., Coconut Latte).\n\n## 2. Unit Economics & Cost Structure Matrix\n\n| Cost Structure Ratio | Starbucks Flagship | Luckin Grab-and-Go | Independent Cafe (Ref) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Cost of Goods Sold (COGS)** | 28% - 32% | 35% - 38% | 30% - 35% |\n| **Rent & Property Fee** | 15% - 18% | 7% - 10% | 18% - 25% |\n| **Labor Cost** | 22% - 25% | 10% - 12% | 20% - 24% |\n| **Fulfillment & Delivery** | 3% - 5% | 12% - 15% | 2% - 4% |\n| **Store Operating Margin (OPM)** | 18% - 22% | 24% - 28% | 10% - 15% |\n\n## 3. Supply Chain & Marketing Insights\n\n1. **Direct Sourcing & Roasting**: Major brands have established origin bean sourcing and automated roasting facilities. See [[Roasting Factory & Origin Sourcing]].\n2. **Product R&D**: Combined with [[Sinking Market Coffee Insights]], leverage signature milk coffee offerings to acquire and retain loyalty members."
